# No Unsolicited Style Changes

When fixing bugs or making functional changes, **do not alter visual design** unless the user explicitly asks for style/UI changes.

## Rules

- Fix the underlying behavior only (data, logic, loading, conditions).
- Keep existing markup, class names, layout, colors, shapes, spacing, and typography as-is.
- Do not "improve" presentation by borrowing patterns from other components (e.g. wrapping an image in a circular badge) when the task is to make something work.
- If a style change would help, ask first — do not apply it proactively.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — user asked to make the logo show; agent redesigned it
<span className="rounded-full bg-black p-2">
  <img src={logoSrc} className="w-8 h-8 object-contain" />
</span>

// ✅ GOOD — same original markup; only ensure src/data is available
<img src={logoSrc} className="w-16 aspect-video object-cover" />
```
